cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vineclim in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "vineclim: bioclimatic indices and reproducible reports for high-altitude vineyards"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-17"
year: 2026
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/YilongXiao/vineclim"
url: "https://github.com/YilongXiao/vineclim"
authors:
  - family-names: Xiao
    given-names: Yilong
    email: YilongXiao@users.noreply.github.com
abstract: >-
  vineclim computes growing degree days (GDD10), the Huglin heliothermal
  index, cool night index, frost days, hot days, growing-season length and
  growing-season diurnal range from daily minimum and maximum temperature.
  It reads station CSV files or NASA POWER grid downloads, flags years with
  more than 20 percent missing data as insufficient_data, and writes JSON,
  CSV, a Markdown report and figures. Elevation correction by a constant
  lapse rate is optional and always reported next to uncorrected values.
keywords:
  - viticulture
  - bioclimatic indices
  - growing degree days
  - huglin index
  - frost
  - high-altitude vineyards
  - nasa power
  - reproducible research
